  "query_preview": "..\nTropical Storm Rachel has now transitioned to a Post Tropical\nCyclone. Rachel will move rapidly NE into the Desert Southwest \nwell W/NW of our CWA this morning, but will still bring us \nstrong gusty winds and a continued threat for isolated strong to\nsevere thunderstorms the rest of the night. SFC winds are also \nincreasing as the remnant wind field pushes into our CWA. \nStrongest winds are across the higher elevations and from \ncentral Pima County west into western Pima County. Highest gusts\nhave been in the 35-45 mph range. These gusts may top out close\nto 55 mph in the Wind Adv area and could approach 60 mph in \nconvection. No changes were made to the ADV tonight. \n\nContinued rain chances are expected today with the possibility\nof isolated thunderstorms. However, no severe weather is\nexpected as the atmosphere becomes more stable through the day. \n\nSoutherly flow ahead of the longwave trough will linger keeping\nchances for rain and thunderstorms 20-50% for Monday and \nTuesday. Drier air returns by Wednesday, clearing out shower \nactivity across the area. Expect an extended period of below- \nnormal temperatures starting Sunday and persisting through mid- \nweek.\n\nWe are still watching for a late week Easterly Wind Event, which\ncould bring widespread Wind Adv criteria to much of the CWA, \nespecially easterly wind prone areas.",
